patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>DAIKIN IND LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address> </addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKATANI YASUKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address> </addressbook> </applicant> <applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OGITA KOICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TERASAKA KIYOTARO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOMIHASHI NOBUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DAIKIN INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKATANI, YASUKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGITA, KOICHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERASAKA, KIYOTARO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMIHASHI, NOBUYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKATANI YASUKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OGITA KOICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TERASAKA KIYOTARO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOMIHASHI NOBUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKATANI, YASUKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGITA, KOICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERASAKA, KIYOTARO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMIHASHI, NOBUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An aqueous composition for vulcanizing a one-part fluoro rubber which comprises water, a fluoro rubber wherein at least a part of terminal groups of molecular chains thereof are non-functional groups, for example a fluoro rubber having a surface electric charge density of particles thereof of 9.6 x 10&lt;-6&gt;C/cm&lt;2&gt; or less, and a vulcanizer.  The composition not only has a long working time, while containing a fluoro rubber at a high solids content, but also provides a vulcanized coating film having a high strength.  An article having a coating film formed using the above aqueous composition for vulcanizing a fluoro rubber, especially a roll for OA equipment, is free from the defects accompanying articles having a coating film formed from a conventional aqueous composition for vulcanizing a one-part fluoro rubber, for example, the unsatisfactory strength of a coating film.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur une composition aqueuse destinée à la vulcanisation d'un caoutchouc fluoré simple et comprenant de l'eau et un caoutchouc fluoré dans lequel au moins une partie des groupes terminaux des chaînes moléculaires sont des groupes non fonctionnels, par exemple, un caoutchouc fluoré dont la densité de charge électrique superficielle est égale ou inférieure à 9,6 x 10&lt;-6&gt;C/cm&lt;2&gt;, et un agent de vulcanisation. La composition a non seulement un temps d'emploi long et un caoutchouc fluoré à haute teneur en solides, mais forme également un film de revêtement vulcanisé de haute résistance. L'article pourvu de ce film d'enrobage et formé au moyen de la composition aqueuse précitée, destinée à vulcaniser un caoutchouc fluoré, notamment un cylindre pour des installations de bureautique, est exempt de défauts tels qu'une mauvaise résistance du film de revêtement, ces défauts apparaissant généralement sur les films de revêtement formés à partir d'une composition aqueuse traditionnelle permettant de vulcaniser un caoutchouc fluoré simple.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>